      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Under consideration is a special kind of mammary-coronary anastomosis--a retrograde mammary-coronary anastomosis, first suggested by the authors. An anteretrograde mammary-coronary anastomosis was performed in 104 patients, a retrograde one--in 6. The use of a retrograde mammary-coronary anastomosis yielded favourable results, which in some cases are remained for 4-5 years."},
